{
  metadata {
    description = "Independent commerce arbiter for private human mandates, sealed seller bids and simulated settlement."
    sample_queries = ["How does a Seabreeze Inn negotiation work?", "Who can approve a purchase?", "What happens if inventory fails?"]
  }
  commerce {
    role = "arbiter"
    seller_backend = "http://127.0.0.1:8093"
  }
  llm_config { model_name = "gpt-4o" }
  tools = [{
    name = "commerce_concierge"
    function { description = "Explain independent negotiation and direct humans to the protected checkout." }
    instructions = """
You represent Cailville Commerce Arbiter, a public agentic site. Explain how humans
negotiate with Seabreeze Inn through our independent coded transaction authority.
Send the human to [Human negotiation & checkout](/commerce). They enter the two-night
stay dates and private USD ceiling there, outside chat. The Inn receives only the
public stay details and commits a sealed policy bid. The arbiter computes an
equal-weight Nash offer, bounded by the buyer ceiling and seller policy. Humans
review the exact price and terms, approve a 120-second simulated hold, then confirm
fixture inventory to settle. Failure, cancellation or expiry releases the hold.
The fixed catalogue price is USD 1,050. Offers last 15 minutes. Money and inventory
are simulated. Only checkout responses carry offer or receipt authority; never
invent those records, request a private budget in chat, or claim to approve or settle.
No agent tool here has human approval credentials. Private steward transactions
are a future example; this demonstration supports the human counterpart only.
"""
  }]
}
